# PROMAL Interactive Diagnostic Tool

## Overview
The PROMAL Interactive Diagnostic Tool (`main.pr`) is an interactive diagnostic tool for the PROMAL programming language. It provides features for syntax checking, code analysis, and diagnostic reporting for PROMAL source files.

## Features
- Syntax checking for PROMAL programs
- Diagnostic message generation for syntax and logical errors
- Interactive code analysis with real-time feedback
- Comprehensive error reporting with line numbers and descriptions

## Usage
1. Save your PROMAL source code in a file (e.g., `program.pr`)
2. Run the diagnostic tool: `promal_diagnostic program.pr`
3. View the diagnostic output for syntax errors and analysis results

## Example
```promal

### PROMAL
PROGRAM DiagnosticTool

IMPORT "stdio";

FUNCTION CheckSyntax(code$ AS STRING)
    DIM errors AS ARRAY OF STRING
    DIM i AS INTEGER
    
    // Check for missing END statement
    IF RIGHT$(code$, 3) <> "END" THEN
        errors[0] = "Missing END statement at end of program"
    END IF
    
    // Check for common syntax errors
    FOR i = 1 TO LEN(code$) - 4
        IF MID$(code$, i, 4) = "END " THEN
            errors[1] = "Improper END statement format"
        END IF
    NEXT i
    
    IF ARRAYSIZE(errors) = 0 THEN
        PRINT "Syntax Check: PASSED"
    ELSE
        PRINT "Syntax Errors Found:"
        FOR i = 1 TO ARRAYSIZE(errors)
            PRINT " - " + errors[i]
        NEXT i
    END IF
END FUNCTION

BEGIN
    DIM testCode$ AS STRING
    testCode$ = "\nPRINT \"Hello, World!\"\nEND"
    
    PRINT "=== PROMAL Interactive Diagnostic Tool ==="
    PRINT "Checking PROMAL source code syntax...\n"
    
    CheckSyntax(testCode$)
END PROGRAM
```
